  "estimand": "The causal effect of a teammate DRIVE possession immediately preceding a PNR possession (by the same team) on the PNR PPP of the subsequent PNR possession. Alternatively, the effect of a DRIVE action within a PNR possession on that PNR possession's PPP.",
  "unit": "Possession (specifically, a PNR possession).",
  "sample": "All PNR possessions from NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25, and 2025-26 (regular season and playoffs, excluding garbage time). Each PNR possession will be categorized based on whether it was immediately preceded by a teammate DRIVE possession (by the same team) or not. If focusing on within-possession events, all PNR possessions where a DRIVE action precedes the PNR action within the same possession.",
  "power": "The study should aim for 80% power to detect a 0.05 PPP difference (e.g., from 0.85 to 0.90 PPP) with an alpha of 0.05. This would require a sufficient number of PNR possessions in both the 'preceded by DRIVE' and 'not preceded by DRIVE' groups. A minimum of 500 PNR possessions in each group is a rough heuristic, but a formal power calculation will be performed based on observed variance and expected effect size.",
  "controls": "Statistical controls will be applied to account for potential confounding factors: team offensive rating, opponent defensive rating, game state (score differential, quarter), PNR initiator identity, PNR screener identity, and season. A player-level fixed effects model could be used if sufficient data per player exists.",
  "falsification": "A falsification test could involve examining whether a teammate DRIVE *following* a PNR (if such a sequence can be meaningfully defined) has any impact on PNR PPP, which would not be expected. Another test could be to examine the effect of a random, unrelated play type preceding a PNR.",
  "multiplicity": "No explicit multiplicity correction planned if only testing the single hypothesis as stated. If multiple alternative definitions of 'preceding' or other play types are explored, Bonferroni or False Discovery Rate (FDR) correction will be applied.",
  "decision_rule": "The hypothesis will be considered supported if the estimated coefficient for 'preceded by teammate DRIVE' is positive and statistically significant (p < 0.05) in the primary analysis, after controlling for confounders. The magnitude of the effect should also be practically meaningful (e.g., >0.02 PPP).",
